@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Knowledge base ingestion (customer-managed vector knowledge base) — UML activity diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : diagrams/mermaid/06-knowledge-base-ingestion-pipeline.md (views B and C)
' Chapter            : 01-amazon-bedrock/knowledge-bases/04-ingestion-parsing-chunking.md
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      AWS documents the stages, permissions and statuses, not how
'                      Bedrock schedules the work: the Bedrock lane is a conceptual
'                      model of documented behaviour. No AWS icons; no network includes.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-data-source-sync-ingest.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-chunking-parsing.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-advanced-parsing.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-custom-transformation.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/knowledge-bases-logging.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/kb-permissions.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/encryption-kb.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_agent_StartIngestionJob.html
'
' What UML adds over the Mermaid view: one decision per document, swimlanes for
' who acts, and the end-of-job decision a pipeline must make.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title Knowledge base ingestion — one sync of a customer-managed vector knowledge base (UML activity)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #555555
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888
skinparam swimlaneWidth same

|#E8F1FB|Scheduler or pipeline step\nIAM role|
start
:StartIngestionJob (knowledgeBaseId, dataSourceId)
HTTPS · SigV4 · bedrock:StartIngestionJob; <<#E8F1FB>>

|#E6F4EA|Amazon Bedrock ingestion job\nevery call uses the knowledge base service role|
:Return HTTP 202 · ingestionJobId · status STARTING; <<#E6F4EA>>
note right
  Only one job runs per data source
  and per knowledge base at a time
end note
:sts:AssumeRole on the knowledge base service role
trust: bedrock.amazonaws.com · aws:SourceAccount · aws:SourceArn; <<#FDECEA>>
:Job IN_PROGRESS
log StatusChanged · INGESTION_JOB_STARTED; <<#E6F4EA>>
:List the bucket prefix; read documents and .metadata.json files
s3:ListBucket · s3:GetObject; <<#E6F4EA>>
note right
  Transient data is encrypted with your key
  (kms:GenerateDataKey, kms:Decrypt) when the data source
  sets serverSideEncryptionConfiguration.kmsKeyArn
end note

while (Next document in the bucket?) is (yes)
  switch (What changed for this document since the last sync?)
  case (new, or content changed)
    :Parse the whole file
    default parser (text only) · BEDROCK_DATA_AUTOMATION
    · BEDROCK_FOUNDATION_MODEL (InvokeModel); <<#E6F4EA>>
    :Chunk the text
    default · fixed · hierarchical · semantic · none; <<#E6F4EA>>
    if (Transformation function configured?\nPOST_CHUNKING) then (yes)
      :Write chunk files to your intermediate S3 location; <<#EDE7F6>>
      :Invoke your AWS Lambda function with file references; <<#FDEBD0>>
      :Read back rewritten chunks or chunk-level metadata; <<#EDE7F6>>
    else (no)
    endif
    :bedrock:InvokeModel on the embedding model for every chunk; <<#E6F4EA>>
    if (Embedding failed?) then (yes)
      :Log ResourceStatusChanged · EMBEDDING_FAILED
      with status_reasons; <<#FFF8E1>>
      note right
        Counted in statistics.numberOfDocumentsFailed;
        the job does not fail. Our reading: the document
        is not in the index and is processed again next sync
      end note
    else (no)
      :Write vectors, chunk text and metadata to your vector store
      a changed document is re-indexed in full; <<#EDE7F6>>
      :Log ResourceStatusChanged · INDEXED; <<#FFF8E1>>
    endif
  case (only its metadata file changed\nnot CSV · no transformation function)
    :Read its vectors, merge the new metadata, write back
    no embedding model call; <<#EDE7F6>>
    :Log METADATA_UPDATE_COMPLETED; <<#FFF8E1>>
  case (deleted from the bucket)
    :Delete its vectors from your vector store; <<#EDE7F6>>
    :Log DELETED; <<#FFF8E1>>
  case (unchanged)
    :Skip; <<#E6F4EA>>
  endswitch
endwhile (no more documents)

if (Job-level error?\nfor example the role cannot reach the store) then (yes)
  :Job FAILED with failureReasons; <<#FDECEA>>
else (no)
  :Job COMPLETE
  statistics include numberOfDocumentsFailed; <<#E6F4EA>>
endif

|Scheduler or pipeline step\nIAM role|
:GetIngestionJob until COMPLETE, FAILED or STOPPED
bedrock:GetIngestionJob; <<#E8F1FB>>
if (FAILED, or numberOfDocumentsFailed > 0?) then (yes)
  :Treat the run as failed
  read failureReasons and the EMBEDDING_FAILED log entries; <<#FDECEA>>
  note right: Academy recommendation
else (no)
  :Wait before querying: new vectors can take a few minutes
  to become searchable in stores other than Amazon Aurora; <<#E8F1FB>>
endif
stop

floating note left
  StopIngestionJob at any point: STOPPING, then STOPPED.
  Start again later to ingest the rest.
  RESOURCE_IGNORED: a document was not processed;
  the reason is in status_reasons.
  A metadata file for doc.pdf must be named
  doc.pdf.metadata.json. CSV files are always
  re-ingested when their metadata changes.
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | rounded box | action |
  | diamond | decision on documented behaviour |
  | swimlane | who performs the action |
  |<#E8F1FB> blue | caller |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | Amazon Bedrock (managed) |
  |<#FDEBD0> orange | your compute |
  |<#EDE7F6> purple | read or write of data at rest (bucket, vector store) |
  |<#FDECEA> red | security control or failure |
  |<#FFF8E1> yellow | log record — only with APPLICATION_LOGS delivery enabled |
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
